nCrunchTemp_*

# ---------- Visual Studio ----------
# .vs/ is the big one — per-developer window layout, editor state and the
# SQLite database VS uses for IntelliSense. It changes constantly and is the
# usual cause of "conflict in a file I never opened".
.vs/
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.userprefs
*.sln.docstates
*.sln.ide/
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.VC.VC.opendb
*.cachefile
*.dbmdl
*.jfm
.vshistory/
.localhistory/
*.svclog
*.scc

# MSBuild / profiler output
msbuild.log
msbuild.err
msbuild.wrn
*.binlog
*.tlog
*.psess
*.vsp
*.vspx
*.sap

# ReSharper / Rider plugins inside VS
_ReSharper*/
*.[Rr]e[Ss]harper
*.DotSettings.user
.sonarqube/

# ---------- VS Code ----------
# Ignore everything personal, but keep the four files worth sharing so the
# whole team gets the same formatting and debug config.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/
.ionide/
*.code-workspace

# ---------- JetBrains (Rider / WebStorm) ----------
.idea/
*.iml

# ---------- OS ----------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------- Claude Code / AI assistant ----------
# Personal AI working files. CLAUDE.md is an individual working agreement with
# the assistant (how I want to be taught and helped), not a team standard — so
# it stays local rather than being imposed on everyone else's setup.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
# If the team later wants shared permissions or hooks, un-ignore just that file:
# !.claude/settings.json
